{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/962684-using-forces-in-a-new-way-weaponized-iron-sand","id":962684,"title":"Using Forces in a new way... weaponized Iron Sand.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-02T21:29:26-07:00","id":962684,"title":"Using Forces in a new way... weaponized Iron Sand.","content":"So, a player of mine has come up with a very interesting Spell and a weapon. As you might have guessed from my Legacies post earlier, one of my players is a very Japanese oriented Obrimos. He's also a knack for using Spells in interesting ways (to say the least). Lately he told me about how his character would try to create a katana that could be easily &quot;dismissed&quot;. His idea was to use the Ruling Practice of the Forces Arcanum to control the natural magnetism of lodestone (magnetite) into shaping it onto a katana blade and relinquish the Spell so that the iron sand would remain shaped like the katana, held together by magnetic forces. Then, he could simply recast Control Magnetism to change the shape of the blade into something else as needed (lock-pick, shield, shower of shrapnel...).<br /> <br /> Would the Ruling Practice suffice for the creation of such weapon? I think at least Perfecting to make the magnetism strong enough and then Weaving to make the magnetic force adopt the shape of a blade and maintain enough cohesion to be able to harm... but I want your opinions! :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11807-htaiji","name":"HTaiji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11807_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T21:55:22-07:00","id":962696,"title":"","content":"Well, in physics the Greater Force is markedly stronger than magnetism when it comes to cohesion so the magnetic force would have to be quite powerful to replace it. Weaving seems pretty fitting for the spell in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T22:05:02-07:00","id":962699,"title":"","content":"Physics has little to no relation to magic being functional. That said, I think it would be Perfecting to create a strong enough magnetic force (This is probably a narrative effect unless you want to get nitpicky about it) and then it would be Ruling to change the shape of the magnetic field for it to be a sword or whatever shape. Being a strong magnetic field though it'd be likely to attract other ferrous metals beyond just lodestone sand, and screw up computers that are too close, etc. Basically, yeah it's possible but it might require further effects or Reach to avoid it acting like any super magnet would. That might be fun too though since he could create a Shielding effect that prevents the influence of the blade from expanding beyond his desired application and then if he wants to go really crazy with magnetics he can drop the Shield and wreak magnetic havoc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 09-03-2016, 01:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T22:09:29-07:00","id":962701,"title":"","content":"Cool idea. Magnetite couldn't normally do that so it's not <i>compelling</i>. However it's fundamentally altering its properties (making dust act solid) so it's not <i>ruling</i> either. I think you could make a strong case for <i>perfecting</i> though. I wouldn't go as far as <i>patterning</i>, that seems a bit too high a rating.<br /> <br /> I don't think there's any need to make it two spells. Magic doesn't have to line up perfectly, it can blur the lines and include extra bits to make the spell work. &quot;Use magnetism to make sword&quot; is really just one concept as far as an Imago goes. Although doing it as two spells would be convenient for the caster if he wants to control it later without needing to change an existing spell, so that might be what you've got in mind there. One more permanent perfecting spell to enhance the dust, then more controlled and directed weaving spells to give it particular shapes makes a lot of sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T03:42:37-07:00","id":962754,"title":"","content":"I have a feeling your player is a fan of A certain magical Index. Specifically the esper known as the Railgun. I suggest limiting access to small change.<br /> In that universe she is one of the most powerfull electromasters (Master of Forces) around, so setting the bar for some of her powers a bit high is not really that strange to do. Patterning sounds very appropriate for locking iron sand into place in a specific form that also functions as that form.<br /> Alternatively you could make the Potency the spell be the amount of times that the created item can be used before the spell falls apart. When doing that I would be ok with Weaving as the practice, as it is then close to Platonic Form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12164-zaephyrus","name":"Zaephyrus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T03:59:24-07:00","id":962755,"title":"","content":"I would say Perfecting is the most you would need for such an effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-03T05:36:28-07:00","id":962783,"title":"","content":"I'd say Ruling is probably acceptable, but the quality of the tool would need a Wits + Craft roll to be determined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T02:19:34-07:00","id":964158,"title":"","content":"I would go with perfecting. The difficulty about this isn't mere to create a magnetic force field which is strong enough to hold the iron together, but to limit it to the exact shape of the tool you want to have, so that it doesn't interfere with everything else around it. If you don't limit the force field you would pretty much pull every car down the street to you or more likely lose the grip of the sword.<br /> <br /> On that notion: If you already go with a sword out of magnetic dust, make that dust move. I mean, very fast along the edges. Makes for better cutting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T09:14:26-07:00","id":964326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/962684-using-forces-in-a-new-way-weaponized-iron-sand?p=962783#post962783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say Ruling is probably acceptable, but the quality of the tool would need a Wits + Craft roll to be determined.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It wouldn't require a mundane skill roll to determine the effects of a magical spell. It'd be the potency of the spell that can be used to increase durability, structure and equipment bonus (which is what encompasses quality mechanically.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T21:51:36-07:00","id":964779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zaephyrus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/962684-using-forces-in-a-new-way-weaponized-iron-sand?p=962754#post962754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a feeling your player is a fan of A certain magical Index. Specifically the esper known as the Railgun. I suggest limiting access to small change.<br /> In that universe she is one of the most powerfull electromasters (Master of Forces) around, so setting the bar for some of her powers a bit high is not really that strange to do. Patterning sounds very appropriate for locking iron sand into place in a specific form that also functions as that form.<br /> Alternatively you could make the Potency the spell be the amount of times that the created item can be used before the spell falls apart. When doing that I would be ok with Weaving as the practice, as it is then close to Platonic Form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Misaka Mikoto is a Mortal with Electrokinesis, pretty much anything she does should be replicable with Forces 2, <i>maybe</i> Forces 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T01:57:52-07:00","id":964857,"title":"","content":"Is it just me, or does this all seem like it would be easier to make this a Forces/Matter spell instead of just trying to shove it all into Forces? Having Forces to gather all this magnetic material into a shape, and then Matter to make that shape a useful tool, seems much easier than trying to use Forces to pull a bunch of iron into the shape of a sword and then also strengthen all of that into a functional sword.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T02:16:40-07:00","id":964861,"title":"","content":"If you did it with Matter you wouldn't need Forces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T02:47:09-07:00","id":964865,"title":"","content":"You can certainly do it with Matter alone, but there would be a solid case for lower levels of both combined rather than high levels of one if you wanted to go that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T02:57:02-07:00","id":964868,"title":"","content":"At most it would take Matter or Forces 3 either of which any Mage can start with, so the argument that you can use lower levels of both combined isn't really a reduction in difficulty to the task. This is especially true since if you did combine Matter and Forces you'd still need Forces 3 in order to Perfect a magnetic field to be strong enough to hold the lodestone sand in a solid mass.<br /> <br /> I would agree though that Matter is needed to give it additional benefits that only Matter grants, such as 9-again or equipment bonuses though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 09-07-2016, 06:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T04:47:25-07:00","id":964893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/962684-using-forces-in-a-new-way-weaponized-iron-sand?p=964868#post964868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At most it would take Matter or Forces 3 either of which any Mage can start with, so the argument that you can use lower levels of both combined isn't really a reduction in difficulty to the task. This is especially true since if you did combine Matter and Forces you'd still need Forces 3 in order to Perfect a magnetic field to be strong enough to hold the lodestone sand in a solid mass.<br /> <br /> I would agree though that Matter is needed to give it additional benefits that only Matter grants, such as 9-again or equipment bonuses though.</div> </div> </div> </div>And therefore, you shouldn't do a static magnetic field, but one in flux. You can't replicate magnetic particles moving at the speed of sound (or faster) along the edges of your sword with matter. If you do this fast enough the particles should even start glowing, making for a nice light saber. Would be pretty warm too. Probably not that suble though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T07:27:04-07:00","id":964945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/962684-using-forces-in-a-new-way-weaponized-iron-sand?p=964779#post964779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Misaka Mikoto is a Mortal with Electrokinesis, pretty much anything she does should be replicable with Forces 2, <i>maybe</i> Forces 3.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I disagree with you on that. Remember that she is capable of instantly generating enough electricity to fire Thunderbolt (Forces 4) equivalents. Plus she is capable of clinging to walls by a highly amplified static cling effect, which I would at least classify as Forces 3. Yes, a similar effect can be created with Alter Gravity (Forces 2), but she uses a different method which has a higher Forces equivalent.<br /> It would be under that same category that I would place the sword made out of iron sand. If some kind of spool is used to focus the sand around I would agree with Forces 2, but then it would be easier to just carry around an actual sword.<br /> <br /> I do agree with you that her clones would fall within Forces 2 at a maximum.<br /> If you want to continue this discussion then I suggest we create a different topic to keep this one focussed on its original question. I might do that anyway when I have a bit more time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/19.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12164-zaephyrus","name":"Zaephyrus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T07:47:43-07:00","id":964954,"title":"","content":"I'm really surprised no one's brought up the idea of pocket sand.<br /> <br /> It seems like you could just have a pocket of regular sand that you throw at people and use Forces to make hit like a hundred bullets or a thousand mile per hour wind of glass shards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-07-2016, 10:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T08:24:01-07:00","id":964968,"title":"","content":"Namely because the idea is to use the magnetic fields to shape these granular lodestones into more than just a weapon. A sword just happened to be an example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T14:22:32-07:00","id":965265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/962684-using-forces-in-a-new-way-weaponized-iron-sand?p=964868#post964868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At most it would take Matter or Forces 3 either of which any Mage can start with, so the argument that you can use lower levels of both combined isn't really a reduction in difficulty to the task. This is especially true since if you did combine Matter and Forces you'd still need Forces 3 in order to Perfect a magnetic field to be strong enough to hold the lodestone sand in a solid mass.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't see how Forces 3 could do this alone. A bunch of magnetic particles in the shape of a sword is not a sword. A strong enough magnetic field to actually force the particles to have the rigidity of steel, and hold an edge, would be insanely immense with all sorts of side effects unless your using even more magic to constrain that as well (beyond being so strong you're risking other metal objects flying at you, there's also the risk of pulling them together so strongly they fuse and then can't be reformed by ending the spell). Otherwise you swing your sword (or twist your screwdriver, or whatever) and it falls apart because small magnetic particles have extremely poor sheering resistance (aka you can separate powerful magnets far more easily by sliding them against each other instead of pulling them apart).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T14:27:03-07:00","id":965268,"title":"","content":"Perfecting would do it. I agree about the risk of creating such a strong magnetic field, if you look at my past posts in this thread you'll see one that suggests handling it with a Shielding effect so the magnetic field is contained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T15:20:20-07:00","id":965294,"title":"","content":"The problem is that Perfecting magnetism isn't going to create or replace the molecular bonds required to make a function tool out of fine grain magnetic particles. It's going to make the particles take the shape of the sword/screwdriver/etc. but that's not going to make a functional tool. I'd also have a lot of problems with letting Forces control molecular bonding directly.<br /> <br /> And, again, shielding against stuff flying at you is only one such issue. It doesn't address that squeezing metal together so hard like that causes it to weld together and thus defeat the purpose of being able to have &quot;sand&quot; you can reconfigure at will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T15:33:46-07:00","id":965300,"title":"","content":"Try not to science magic too much and it will work much better and fluid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T15:40:57-07:00","id":965306,"title":"","content":"Actually, why couldn't Forces control the energy that maintains a molecular bond? With Zoom In you can witness that bond, I think that would be enough to make it energy that can be used as a subject for a spell. It would also make that Reach option more useful.<br /> <br /> Alternatively to a sand sword held together with Forces you could simply shape telekinetic energy to fit your purpose via Weaving.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T16:42:25-07:00","id":965331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/962684-using-forces-in-a-new-way-weaponized-iron-sand?p=965300#post965300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Try not to science magic too much and it will work much better and fluid.</div> </div> </div> </div>While true to an extent, the issue comes in when people are, in-character, combining magic and science. Because why not? If you know the science of how something works, and you can use magic, it makes sense that you'd try to combine those to things.<br /> <br /> That's basically the premise of the thread when it comes to using magnetism to control grains of metal, and then try to form it into tools.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/962684-using-forces-in-a-new-way-weaponized-iron-sand?p=965306#post965306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, why couldn't Forces control the energy that maintains a molecular bond?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because that basically means Forces can do anything Matter can do except Making. Directly manipulating atomic bond energies lets you pretty much do any Matter effect with Forces because those bond energies are what dictate the properties of Matter.<br /> <br /> It also starts infringing on Life fairly significantly as well. Once Forces turns into complete control of physics, it turns into control of chemistry (which is applied physics), and turns into control of biology (which is applied physics and chemistry).<br /> <br /> If Forces and Matter are meant to be two separate things, you can't give Forces direct control over the fundamental physical properties that make Matter things &quot;matter&quot; to Forces.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alternatively to a sand sword held together with Forces you could simply shape telekinetic energy to fit your purpose via Weaving. </div> </div> </div>Why even bother with the sand at this point? Just TK things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T17:33:11-07:00","id":965359,"title":"","content":"On that last part, pretty much my point.<br /> <br /> As to your other points, I'd draw the line at fine tuning things too much. For instance I'd allow Forces to dissolve or strengthen the energy in molecular bonds, but that doesn't mean I'd let Forces give equipment bonuses to equipment or fine tune genetic structures. I mean sure, technically, under the purview of science everything is energy on some level, but we've got 10 arcana and while Forces might let us fudge the numbers a bit you've got to respect that if you're going to run a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T19:38:47-07:00","id":965429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/962684-using-forces-in-a-new-way-weaponized-iron-sand?p=965306#post965306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, why couldn't Forces control the energy that maintains a molecular bond?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly because there isn't an energy that maintains a molecular bond... well unless you're talking the Van Der Waal force, but that's not really molecular per se and is much more of a geochemistry thing. <br /> <br /> Ionic and Covalent bonding, which are what are generally considered molecular bonds, are particles finding probability distributions at which all interacting energy values are balanced. While those energy values themselves could potentially be manipulated, it would be a very indirect method of altering the physical properties of a substance and unlikely to have many useful applications.<br /> <br /> The most useful technique of doing this is to heat up the object, which is a pretty common technique already for Oubrimos. Alternatively a Forces mage could probably ionize substances pretty effectively too. Wouldn't really be able to do the same sorts of things a Matter mage could manage though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T20:23:52-07:00","id":965447,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure that's the point I was making.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T20:29:03-07:00","id":965451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zaephyrus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/962684-using-forces-in-a-new-way-weaponized-iron-sand?p=964945#post964945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I disagree with you on that. Remember that she is capable of instantly generating enough electricity to fire Thunderbolt (Forces 4) equivalents.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, first, thunder is sound, lightning is electricity. Second, Lightning Bolt is patterning, it turns external, ambient energy into a blast of electricity. Third, I specified she's a Mortal with Electrokinesis (which does allow generating the energy-type in question), the actual <i>control</i> is only Forces 2. With an energy source a Forces 2 mage can shoot lightning at people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus she is capable of clinging to walls by a highly amplified static cling effect, which I would at least classify as Forces 3. Yes, a similar effect can be created with Alter Gravity (Forces 2), but she uses a different method which has a higher Forces equivalent. </div> </div> </div>I did say &quot;maybe Forces 3&quot; in my initial post. But, with Mikoto specifically I'd say it would still only be Forces 2 since she passively generates the electricity from herself, making her part of the circuit. A mage would need Forces 3 to do this because Mikoto's electricity generation simply falls outside the Mage template (which makes sense, she's not a Mage she's an Esper - a Mortal with Electrokinesis).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It would be under that same category that I would place the sword made out of iron sand. If some kind of spool is used to focus the sand around I would agree with Forces 2, but then it would be easier to just carry around an actual sword. </div> </div> </div>Misaka acts as part of the circuit, but yes an actual sword would be easier to carry around <i>if you ignore social stigma and local laws.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I do agree with you that her clones would fall within Forces 2 at a maximum. </div> </div> </div>This is another misunderstanding on your part - the MISAKA are less not less <i>versatile</i> inherently (lowers dots in Forces), they're less <i>powerful</i> which leads to less versatility (lower dots in Gnosis for a Mage).<br /> <br /> But, again, it'd be better to model Misaka Mikoto as a Mortal with Electrokinesis 5; the difference between her and the MISAKA would be that Mikoto would have higher Resolve, higher Occult, and more Specializations/merits that enhanced her dicepool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T15:42:11-07:00","id":966959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/962684-using-forces-in-a-new-way-weaponized-iron-sand?p=965447#post965447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure that's the point I was making.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it was, I agree with your point.<br /> <br /> Please forgive the pedantry, I was just addressing some of the vocabulary there to expand upon the specifics and provide the details about why your point was correct. Sorry that was a little unclear, I didn't explain it very well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}